The transformer (esbuild, or oxc in rolldown-vite) can strip comments before V8 coverage maps them back to the source. Ignore hints can disappear this way. The Vitest coverage docs suggest adding `@preserve` to the hint:

```ts
try {
  console.log('test')
} catch (err) /* v8 ignore next -- @preserve */ {
  console.error(err)
}
```

Please try that and check the "Ignoring code" section of the coverage guide (`docs/guide/coverage.md`).

Your snippet also has a syntax problem: the `try` block is missing its closing `}`. It also calls `consolr.error`, which looks like a typo.

If `@preserve` doesn't help, please share a minimal repro (a StackBlitz or a small repo) with your `vitest.config` and the output of a coverage run. Then we can treat it as a rolldown-vite bug.
